I'll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the data files.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Now let me examine the data files to understand their structure and content.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/folder_manifest.txt"
  }
}
```

Now let me examine the two CSV files to understand their structure.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/site_daily_kwh.csv"
  }
}
```

Now let me check the field operations export file.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/field_ops_export.csv"
  }
}
```

I notice there are some data quality issues in the field_ops_export.csv file. There's a row with an empty date and unit T-01 with value 9999, and another row with an invalid date "13/37/2024". Let me first create a Python script to analyze and merge these datasets. First, let me check what Python packages are available.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "python --version"
  }
}
```

Good. Now let me create a directory structure for my analysis and start writing the analysis script.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir -p code outputs report/images"
  }
}
```

Let me try with Windows commands since this appears to be a Windows system.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "mkdir code outputs report\\images"
  }
}
```

Now let me run this script to see the initial data exploration.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analyze_telemetry.py"
  }
}
```

I need to adjust the path since we're running from the code directory. Let me fix the script.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/analyze_telemetry.py",
    "old_str": "# Load site daily kWh data\nsite_df = pd.read_csv('data/site_daily_kwh.csv')",
    "new_str": "# Load site daily kWh data\nsite_df = pd.read_csv('../data/site_daily_kwh.csv')"
  }
}
```


```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/analyze_telemetry.py",
    "old_str": "# Load field operations export data\n# Note: There's a BOM character in the first column name, and some data quality issues\nfield_df = pd.read_csv('data/field_ops_export.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')",
    "new_str": "# Load field operations export data\n# Note: There's a BOM character in the first column name, and some data quality issues\nfield_df = pd.read_csv('../data/field_ops_export.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the script again.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analyze_telemetry.py"
  }
}
```

The error is because there's a NaN value in the ReadingDt column. Let me update the script to handle this better and continue with data cleaning.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/analyze_telemetry.py",
    "old_str": "# Check date ranges\nprint(f\"\\nDate range in site data: {site_df['record_date'].min()} to {site_df['record_date'].max()}\")\nprint(f\"Date range in field data: {field_df['ReadingDt'].min()} to {field_df['ReadingDt'].max()}\")",
    "new_str": "# Check date ranges\nprint(f\"\\nDate range in site data: {site_df['record_date'].min()} to {site_df['record_date'].max()}\")\n# Filter out rows with missing dates in field data for date range calculation\nfield_valid_dates = field_df[field_df['ReadingDt'].notna()]['ReadingDt']\nprint(f\"Date range in field data (valid dates only): {field_valid_dates.min()} to {field_valid_dates.max()}\")\n\n# Display problematic rows in field data\nprint(f\"\\nProblematic rows in field data:\")\nprint(field_df[field_df['ReadingDt'].isna()])\nprint(f\"\\nRows with potentially invalid dates:\")\n# Check for rows that might have invalid date formats\nfor idx, row in field_df.iterrows():\n    if pd.notna(row['ReadingDt']):\n        try:\n            datetime.strptime(row['ReadingDt'], '%m/%d/%Y')\n        except ValueError:\n            print(f\"Row {idx}: {row['ReadingDt']} - Invalid date format\")\n"
  }
}
```


```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analyze_telemetry.py"
  }
}
```

Let me check if all the images were created properly.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report\\images"
  }
}
```

Perfect! All images have been created. Let me also check the outputs directory to ensure all intermediate files are there.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir outputs"
  }
}
```

Excellent! All deliverables have been created. Let me do a final check by reading a snippet of the report to ensure it's properly formatted.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "report/report.md"
  }
}
```
